# Golden vectors of func_80047F30 (gDrawInGameHud), the in-game HUD call sequence.
#
# Generated by running the ORIGINAL src/game/80047F30.c together with the ORIGINAL
# src/game/8001C214.c in a host harness; only the MIPS register/asm attributes were stripped and
# the drawing primitives are stubs that record their arguments. The RECT records are therefore
# already halved and colour-widened by the retail rectangle routine itself, so the values below are
# what the PS1 would have put into the primitive packet.
#
# A CASE line carries the input state (retail block fields), the indented lines are the draw calls in
# order. Keys follow the retail offsets: screen = D_8009FA00, players = D_8009FA0C, frame =
# D_8009FAA4; w58/w5c/w64/w326/a4/ae/c1 are player block fields, score0/score1/count1..4/
# total1/total2/stage/mode belong to D_8009FA94; second/secondmax/extraa4/extraa8 describe the
# second game block D_8009F9EC.
#
#   MARKER / SLOTSBAR / TARGETPASS / MARKERS  calls without arguments
#   BAR x y intensity p3 p4 p5 flag            func_80047BE8 (screen coords, no doubling)
#   RECT r g b x=.. y=.. w=.. h=.. blend=..    func_8001C214, already halved and widened
#   TEXT ".." x y colour                       func_80049100
#
# Regenerate or re-check with tests/host/hud/hud_test.sh (that script --emit prints the observed
# output; without it the script compares this file against a fresh run of the retail routine).
#
# Three harness stubs stand in for details that are not in the C code:
#   * func_80049340 is strlen * 4, doubled - the retail advances live in a VRAM glyph atlas that is not
#     decoded. 4 is the port's value and the only number this file cannot prove; 8 is disproved
#     because it puts "Close-Up Side Camera" at x -12.
#   * func_8008CD30 is a printf clone (8008CD3C.c) with 32-bit arguments; the host libc reproduces it
#     once the "l" length modifier is dropped, so "%03ld" prints -05 for -5 just like the PS1 would.
#   * the label table has seven entries, exactly as the retail pointer table at 0x8009AC58 (reached
#     through D_8009F348, sentinel 0x0001FFFF at index 7); a larger index yields an empty string here
#     because the harness cannot reproduce the retail out-of-range read.

CASE A_mode0_60of100 screen=4 players=1 frame=16 health=60 maxhealth=100 w58=65536 w5c=65536 w64=5
  MARKER
  SLOTSBAR
  BAR 15 206 0 89 88 38 0
  TARGETPASS
  MARKERS
CASE B_mode1_full_blink screen=4 players=1 frame=144 health=100 maxhealth=100 w58=65536 w5c=65536 w64=1 score0=1234 count1=2 count2=5 count3=1 count4=3 total1=1 total2=1 mode=1
  MARKER
  SLOTSBAR
  BAR 15 206 0 64 127 64 1
  TARGETPASS
  MARKERS
  RECT 0 0 4 x=281 y=20 w=28 h=10 blend=1
  TEXT "1234" 284 20 9
  RECT 0 0 4 x=279 y=32 w=30 h=10 blend=1
  TEXT "02/05" 282 32 1
  RECT 0 0 4 x=287 y=44 w=22 h=10 blend=1
  TEXT "000" 290 44 3
  RECT 0 0 4 x=279 y=56 w=30 h=10 blend=1
  TEXT "01/03" 282 56 3
